  "boundary": "Actual pinned TvShowsController and shared LibraryController Similar route/action methods, RequestHelpers claim/user selection, native Series/Season selectors, Episode.IsMissingEpisode, UserViewBuilder adjacency, controller paging/error results, actual TVSeriesManager next-up selection, Series/MusicArtist/MusicAlbum/Audio local similar providers, TmdbSeriesSimilarProvider over controlled TMDbLib transport, and SimilarItemsManager provider configuration/order/scoring, remaining-limit queries, exception/cancellation boundaries, remote 20/500 batching, provider-ID resolution and real file cache behavior including exact numeric-string decimal-to-Single midpoint ordering, invalid-string and quoted Single-overflow fallback, and bit-exact Single scoring, with native comparers, actual ASP.NET comma collection and DateTime model binders, actual ExceptionMiddleware, and concrete LibraryManager empty-parent/UserView-parent/Guid.Empty, BaseItemRepository, SimilarItemsManager access filtering, and NextUpService probes over EF Core SQLite. Controlled controller-side repository/manager result arrays, user lookup, DTO projection, local provider results and remote local-library lookup entities are explicit seams. ASP.NET authorization filters, concrete DtoService internals, live external services and deterministic Random shuffle order remain outside this oracle; no public-network call is made. Named or non-finite cache-score rejection is a stricter candidate fail-closed policy and is not asserted as native parity.",
